{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>And for the plague of the garment and of the house.</b> For although both are alike in appearance — greenish or reddish — and both come about in a non-natural manner, nevertheless they differ in this: that which spreads in a garment at the end of the first week is burned entirely, while that which spreads in a house at the end of the first week requires dismantling, scraping, plastering, and is given a further week."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:17.240169345Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}